  "scenario": "A full-time writer and coder is considering the roughly fifty-dollar Royal Kludge RK71 because the listing presents a compact wireless mechanical keyboard with a 75-percent aggregate score across 12 reviews. The buyer wants to know what the listing actually promises, whether same-model hobbyist reports make the board too risky for work, whether general contact-chatter mechanics explain those reports, and what should be checked before keeping or returning it. The available material contains the exact product page, two independently searchable RK71 hobbyist threads, and a general electrical-switch reference, but no licensed months-later RK71 failure study or population failure rate.",
